A) Erodeproofing

This has been a (minor) gripe of mine for some time.  

It bugs me that my rings, wands, and tools can rust, but I can't
de-rust or rustproof them.  I propose:
 
1) !Oil should work on any rusted object, not just weapons and armor.
 
2) A confused reading of ?EW should rustproof anything non-armor
object being wielded, whether or not a weapon.
 
3) A confused reading of ?EA should potentially rustproof worn rings
and amulets.

The effect would be mostly cosmetic, although I guess you could use it
to render your stash chest immune to gelantinous cubes.

B) Silver Armor
 
Also, I think a set of silver gloves and boots would be cool.  They
could either be a random type, like snow boots, or otherwise
non-magical armor.  Obviously, they would be (1) erodeproof, (2) add
silver damage to punches and kicks, as appropriate, and (3) cost a lot
in the shop.
 
